From uaab55242ff4da6c6 at groups.google.com  Wed Feb 17 13:59:04 2021
From: uaab55242ff4da6c6 at groups.google.com (Mike Collyer)
Date: Wed, 17 Feb 2021 13:59:04 +0000
Subject: Re: [geomorph-r-package] Boas Coordinates
Message-ID: <Qzt689gcyz0.mExJgmjhBwAJ@geomorph-r-package.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <Qzt689gcyz0.9T6CKqngBwAJ@geomorph-r-package.groups.google.com>
References: <Qzt689gcyz0.9T6CKqngBwAJ@geomorph-r-package.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/geomorph-r-package/c/Qzt689gcyz0/m/mExJgmjhBwAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Here is how one can do that with one line of code:

boas <- simplify2array(lapply(1:length(Y.gpa$Csize), function(j) Y.gpa$coords[,,j] * Y.gpa$Csize[j]))

Keep in mind that this — as Fred Bookstein suggested to do — is not the same as a Procrustes superimposition without scaling configurations to unit size.  It is scaling, then superimposition, then unscaling.

Cheers!
Mike

